A generic struct is copied per instantiation on a target that emits no type
parameter, as a generic function is: `Box[int]` is a struct `Box__int` with
an int field, so a field read is the bound type rather than Go's `any` or
Kotlin's `Any = null`, which neither compiled. A struct nesting its own
instantiation, `Box[Box[int]]`, names the inner copy, a method on the struct
reads its receiver's copy, and JavaScript keeps the one declaration.

